From: postmarketOS <bramble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: rmnet: use the mainline values for the MAPv5 flags

This vendor copy numbers the rmnet netlink flags differently from mainline:
INGRESS_COALESCE is bit 4 and the MAPv5 checksum flags are bits 5 and 6,
where mainline (and so ModemManager, libqmi and iproute2) has
INGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5 at bit 4 and EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5 at bit 5.

A link created for QMAPv5 downlink checksum offload therefore got
INGRESS_COALESCE instead. The v5 header handler still ran, but
deaggregation did not count the 4-byte checksum header, so every packet
reached the network stack 4 bytes short and was dropped. An egress MAPv5
request turned into an ingress flag, so uplink kept plain QMAP headers.

Use the mainline values and move the vendor-only flags to bits 6 and 7.
All users in the kernel use the symbolic names.

---
--- a/include/uapi/linux/if_link.h	2026-10-23 22:28:04.156229114 +0100
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/if_link.h	2026-10-23 22:28:04.170118760 +0100
@@ -997,9 +997,10 @@
 #define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_MAP_COMMANDS          (1U << 1)
 #define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV4           (1U << 2)
 #define RMNET_FLAGS_EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV4            (1U << 3)
-#define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_COALESCE              (1U << 4)
-#define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5           (1U << 5)
-#define RMNET_FLAGS_EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5            (1U << 6)
+#define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5           (1U << 4)
+#define RMNET_FLAGS_EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV5            (1U << 5)
+/* Vendor flags, kept clear of the mainline bits above */
+#define RMNET_FLAGS_INGRESS_COALESCE              (1U << 6)
 #define RMNET_FLAGS_EGRESS_MAP_CKSUMV3            (1U << 7)
 
 enum {
